# The assets directory is the repo root, so without this the Worker source,
# its config and the git metadata are all published as public static files —
# and Wrangler's dev watcher reload-loops on .git churn.
#
# .wrangler matters as much as the rest: the deploy writes its own build
# output there (including worker.js.map) BEFORE collecting assets, so leaving
# it out published the Worker's source map at
# /.wrangler/tmp/deploy-*/worker.js.map — confirmed live with a 200.
.git
.gitignore
.assetsignore
.wrangler
node_modules
worker.js
wrangler.jsonc
README.md
